 "about_text": "Kaikai Kiki Gallery occupies the basement of an office building in Motoazabu, Tokyo, that once served as the private viewing room for Kaikai Kiki's headquarters. The space was reopened as a public gallery in March 2008, after Kaikai Kiki relocated from a prefab studio in Saitama's Asaka city to Tokyo in 2006. The gallery presents exhibitions of its own roster of Kaikai Kiki artists alongside international figures such as Mark Grotjahn, Matthew Monahan, Seonna Hong and Friedrich Kunath, aiming to build connections between Japanese and international contemporary art. Its stated goal is to manage artists and sell work in a way that gives art new social value, continuing to invite artists from both Japan and abroad to exhibit in its roughly 197 square meter exhibition space.",
 "source_kind": "official",
